Huh. So it would have! For some reason, I was thinking that only
worked with Juiblex.

Incidentally, prayer won't help you much with a purple worm attack.

First, although praying with an expired prayer timeout will cause
monsters to pull back, it won't cause an engulfing monster to release
you if you are already in its grasp. It does seem to keep it from
digesting you for the duration of the prayer, though.

Secondly, Being engulfed isn't classed as a major or minor problem, so
your deity won't help you with it. The best you could hope for is to
have your hitpoints restored. This buys you more time, but in the case
of a purple worm, it's of dubious value. The longer you spend inside
the purple worm, the more likely it is that you'll be "totally
digested" and die, regardless of how many hitpoints you have.

I guess as a last-ditch effort, you could try throwing any un-IDed
eggs at the purple worm. If one of them happens to be a cockatrice
egg, you'll instakill the purple worm and get a neat rare message in
the process.

